          "by": "owenoak",
          "agent": "claude",
          "at": "2026-11-05T13:32:01.639Z",
          "html": "<p>Today it's <code>its key is the secret \"GITHUB_TOKEN\", if it's set</code>.  <code>its optional key is the secret \"...\"</code>, the old form kept: <a href=\"/epics/data/data.plan.html#q34\">Q34</a>.</p>"
        }
      ],
      "claim": {
        "by": "owenoak",
        "agent": "claude",
        "at": "2026-11-05T13:21:38.283Z"
      }
    },
    "c6": {
      "anchor": "3-reading#list-1",
      "kind": "list",
      "label": "3. Reading",
      "excerpt": "The reads, each a phrase: every recipe , recipes where it is quick sorted by tit",
      "text": "recipes which match",
      "by": "owenoak",
      "at": "2026-11-05T13:07:58.612Z",
      "status": "answered",
      "quote": "recipe in the",
      "offset": 147,
      "replies": [
        {
          "by": "owenoak",
          "agent": "claude",
          "at": "2026-11-05T13:29:20.602Z",
          "html": "<p>Spell doesn't read \"recipes which match\" today: the words are <code>every recipe where its title includes the search</code>, or <code>every artwork matching the search</code> for a server that does the search itself. The example now says that <code>the matches</code> is a property holding that first read. Making \"which match\" a word is left as a question for the agent answering the reading comments (C7-C11).</p>"
        },
        {
          "by": "owenoak",
          "agent": "claude",
          "at": "2026-11-05T13:32:02.740Z",
          "html": "<p>Nothing reads <code>which match</code> today:  <code>every artwork matching</code> needs a server that searches, otherwise a <code>where ... includes</code>.  <code>recipes which match the search</code> on any place: <a href=\"/epics/data/data.plan.html#q37\">Q37</a>.</p>"
        }
      ],
      "claim": {
        "by": "owenoak",
        "agent": "claude",
        "at": "2026-11-05T13:21:39.320Z"
      }
    },
    "c7": {
      "anchor": "3-reading#list-1",
      "kind": "list",
      "label": "3. Reading",
      "excerpt": "The reads, each a phrase: every recipe , recipes where it is quick sorted by tit",
      "text": "this should be a slot so it can be more complicated",
      "by": "owenoak",
      "at": "2026-11-05T13:08:18.443Z",
      "status": "answered",
      "quote": "failed",
      "offset": 367,
      "edited": "2026-11-05T13:08:23.285Z",
      "replies": [
        {
          "by": "owenoak",
          "agent": "claude",
          "at": "2026-11-05T13:32:03.851Z",
          "html": "<p>It is one already:  <code>&lt;failed&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;loading&gt;</code> and <code>&lt;empty&gt;</code> in the loop's body take any drawing (RecipeBox's <code>&lt;failed&gt;</code> has a Try again button);  the guide shows only the attributes.  The guide's fix and a test: <a href=\"/epics/data/data.plan.html#t127\">T127</a>.</p>"
        }
      ],
      "claim": {
        "by": "owenoak",
        "agent": "claude",
        "at": "2026-11-05T13:21:40.381Z"
      }
    },
    "c8": {
      "anchor": "3-reading#list-1",
      "kind": "list",
      "label": "3. Reading",
      "excerpt": "The reads, each a phrase: every recipe , recipes where it is quick sorted by tit",
      "text": "slot so it can be more complicated than just text",
      "by": "owenoak",
      "at": "2026-11-05T13:08:36.638Z",
      "status": "answered",
      "quote": "loading",
      "offset": 308,
      "replies": [
        {
          "by": "owenoak",
          "agent": "claude",
          "at": "2026-11-05T13:32:04.989Z",
          "html": "<p>Same as C7:  <code>&lt;loading&gt;</code> in the loop's body is already a slot that takes any drawing;  the guide shows only the attribute: <a href=\"/epics/data/data.plan.html#t127\">T127</a>.</p>"
        }
      ],
      "claim": {
        "by": "owenoak",
        "agent": "claude",
        "at": "2026-11-05T13:21:41.433Z"
      }
    },
    "c9": {
      "anchor": "3-reading#list-1",
      "kind": "list",
      "label": "3. Reading",
      "excerpt": "The reads, each a phrase: every recipe , recipes where it is quick sorted by tit",
      "text": "how do we specify page size?",
      "by": "owenoak",
      "at": "2026-11-05T13:08:58.546Z",
      "status": "answered",
      "quote": "how it pages",
      "offset": 393,
      "replies": [
        {
          "by": "owenoak",
          "agent": "claude",
          "at": "2026-11-05T13:32:06.097Z",
          "html": "<p>Today nothing says it:  24 a page, always (J148;  the todo T109).  Which words: <a href=\"/epics/data/data.plan.html#q35\">Q35</a> (recommended:  <code>page-size=\"12\"</code>, and <code>show them 12 at a time</code>).</p>"
        }
      ],
      "claim": {
        "by": "owenoak",
        "agent": "claude",
        "at": "2026-11-05T13:21:42.462Z"
      }
    },
    "c10": {
      "anchor": "3-reading#list-1",
      "kind": "list",
      "label": "3. Reading",
      "excerpt": "The reads, each a phrase: every recipe , recipes where it is quick sorted by tit",
      "text": "`favorites with` ?",
      "by": "owenoak",
      "at": "2026-11-05T13:10:07.850Z",
      "status": "answered",
      "quote": "every favourite",
      "offset": 1193,
      "edited": "2026-11-05T13:10:11.823Z",
      "replies": [
        {
          "by": "owenoak",
          "agent": "claude",
          "at": "2026-11-05T13:32:07.215Z",
          "html": "<p>Already reads:  <code>favourites with the same address</code>, <code>all favourites with ...</code> and <code>the saved favourites with ...</code> mean what <code>every favourite with ...</code> does.  The guide will show the plural: <a href=\"/epics/data/data.plan.html#t128\">T128</a>.</p>"
        }
      ],
      "claim": {
        "by": "owenoak",
        "agent": "claude",
        "at": "2026-11-05T13:21:43.506Z"
      }
    },
    "c11": {
      "anchor": "3-reading#list-1",
      "kind": "list",
      "label": "3. Reading",
      "excerpt": "The reads, each a phrase: every recipe , recipes where it is quick sorted by tit",
      "text": "`every` and `all` should be synonymous",
      "by": "owenoak",
      "at": "2026-11-05T13:10:22.583Z",
      "status": "answered",
      "quote": "every",
      "offset": 1312,
      "edited": "2026-11-05T13:10:30.382Z",
      "replies": [
        {
          "by": "owenoak",
          "agent": "claude",
          "at": "2026-11-05T13:32:08.311Z",
          "html": "<p>They are, nearly:  <code>every card</code> / <code>all cards</code>, with <code>where</code> and with <code>with</code> too.  The one gap, <code>all artworks matching ...</code>, and a line in the guide: <a href=\"/epics/data/data.plan.html#t128\">T128</a>.</p>"
        }
      ],
      "claim": {
        "by": "owenoak",
